# Side stories (V2-31, docs/DESIGN.md §3.9). Four core ones, 2-5 minutes each, all optional:
#  1. "Back in 5 min": the waiting student in KB1's lobby, there since 9:00, is served once Mme Dupont has her
#     coffee, and says goodnight in chapter 4 (talk.waiting in people.dlg: side_waiting, waiting_bye).
#  2. "Is the sun still yellow?": the piscine survivor in SM14 (talk.student2) comes out to see the sun on rue
#     Pasteur's axis at 18:55 if Mano asks before the twist (survivor_out); he is at the planter wall for the
#     sunset (c2.sunset: survivor_sun) and in cour Pasteur in chapter 5. Asked too late, or never: "I missed it again."
#  3. "Segmentation fault (core dumped)": the SUP asleep in Amphi 4 (talk.sleeper) has a soutenance at 19:00. Wake
#     him in chapter 2 with a spare coffee (the machine owes Mano one once Mme Dupont has hers) or the BDE's
#     babyfoot air horn (world.json spot horn); in chapter 4 he passed, or he asks "Did I miss it?".
#  4. "The duck whisperer": the student who hid the twelve golden ducks (talk.whisperer, cour Pasteur): hints from
#     four ducks, duck zero at twelve.
# Fictional people only; their new lines are silent text (no voice files).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- "Is the sun still yellow?"
~ side.survivor.ask
student2: [#shock] Outside? Like, outdoors?
student2: Give me two minutes. I need to push first.
mano: Rue Pasteur. The planter wall by KB1. Before 18:55.
student2: [#smile] The planter wall. Before 18:55. Got it.
$ set survivor_out
$ clue "The piscine survivor wants to see the sun. Rue Pasteur, KB1's planter wall, before 18:55."

# at the sunset (c2.sunset), when he is there
~ side.survivor.sunset
student2: [#shock] It's... still there. The sun.
student2: Orange, actually. I'll allow it.
student2: [#smile] Eleven hours in SM14. Worth it for seven minutes.
think: Two of us at the planter wall, watching a star leave early. Campus life.
$ set survivor_sun

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- "Segmentation fault (core dumped)"
~ side.sup.coffee
think: Coffee, right under his nose. Hot, bitter, free.
sleeper: [#shock] ...coffee? COFFEE. What time is it?
mano: Nearly seven.
sleeper: [#shock] My soutenance is at 19:00! My slides! My life!
sleeper: [#grin] Thank you, stranger. You smell like a hero.
$ set spare_coffee = false
$ set sup_awake
$ set sup_how = "coffee"
think: He took the coffee with him. Fair.

~ side.sup.horn
$ sfx babyfoot_goal 2
nar: *HOOOONK*
sleeper: [#shock] I'M AWAKE. I'M PRESENTING. What time is it?
mano: Nearly seven.
sleeper: [#shock] My soutenance! 19:00! Why is there a horn?!
sleeper: [#grin] Never mind. Thank you. Terrifying, but thank you.
$ set horn = false
$ set sup_awake
$ set sup_how = "horn"
think: The whole of Amphi 4 is awake now. Sorry, Amphi 4.

# chapter 4: the outcome
~ side.sup.passed
sleeper: [#grin] You! The coffee one! [if sup_how == "coffee"]
sleeper: [#grin] You! The horn one! My ears still ring. [if sup_how == "horn"]
sleeper: [#smile] I passed. Fourteen out of twenty.
sleeper: The jury said I was "surprisingly awake".
think: Segmentation fault: fixed. Somebody else's, for once.
$ set sup_after

~ side.sup.missed
sleeper: [#tired] ...hm? What time is it?
mano: Past nine. At night.
sleeper: [#shock] Did I miss it?
sleeper: [#sad] I missed it. Core dumped.
think: Next time: coffee. Or a horn.
$ set sup_after

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- "The duck whisperer"
~ talk.whisperer
if duck_count >= 12 and not duck_zero
	=> side.ducks.reward
elif duck_zero
	% whisperer: [#smile] Twelve. I still can't believe it.
	% whisperer: [#grin] Duck zero suits you.
	% whisperer: Next year: thirteen. Don't tell anyone.
	=> END
elif duck_count >= 4
	=> side.ducks.hint
elif whisperer_met
	whisperer: [#smirk] {{duck_count}} ducks? Come back at four. Then we talk.
	=> END
whisperer: [#smirk] Ducks? What ducks?
whisperer: ...okay. I hid them. Twelve, golden, since September.
whisperer: Rubber-duck debugging, campus-wide.
whisperer: You explain your bug to a duck. A duck you had to find first.
mano: That's the most EPITA thing I've ever heard.
whisperer: [#grin] Find four and I'll give you hints.
whisperer: Find all twelve and you get duck zero.
$ set whisperer_met
think: A side quest. In the middle of my side quest.

~ side.ducks.hint
whisperer: [#smile] {{duck_count}} ducks. Not bad. A hint, then.
$ duck_hint
$ add duck_hints 1

~ side.ducks.reward
whisperer: [#shock] Twelve. You found all twelve.
whisperer: Nobody finds all twelve. I put one on a car.
mano: It was on the roof. In full view.
whisperer: [#grin] Here. Duck zero. The original. It squeaks in C.
$ set duck_zero
$ set whisperer_met
$ toast "Duck zero" duck
think: My notebook has a duck page now. And I have a duck.
